// A docs board for the HTTP Handler. A Route is wired to a Handler whose code reads the name in
// each request's body and answers with a status and a body built from it. The first request
// carries a name and gets a 200 reply that greets it; the second carries none and gets a 400
// reply that asks for one. The run makes no outbound call.
//
//   row 2:    ROUTE 0, path /hello ===> HTTP HANDLER 1
//   rows 4-5:                              Fault -b3---> SINK 2
//
// The Handler's Fault port, on its bottom middle cell facing south, has a belt to a Debug Sink,
// where a request whose code throws would go. This code never throws, so that belt stays empty.
// The Handler's Out port stays undocked.
//
// One DrawWire mints both cables, request first. Handles mint in command order: the Route 0, the
// Handler 1, the Sink 2, the belt 3, then the cables 4 (request) and 5 (reply). The 9 commands
// and the history seal end the boot on tick 10.
//
// machine_kind u8 legend: ROUTE=9, HTTP HANDLER=10, SINK=7. DrawWire and Dock ports are catalog
// indexes: Route In=0, Out=1; HTTP Handler In=0, Out=1, Fault=2; SINK In=0.
//
// Format 2 adds two fields a page reads and the core never does: `title`, the name a page shows,
// and `captions`, the ticks a viewer pauses on, each with the machine it highlights and one
// sentence about what the board does on that tick.
Board(
    format: 2,
    title: "HTTP Handler",
    seed: 97,
    commands: [
        Place(kind: 9, cell_x: 2, cell_y: 2),        // 0: ROUTE
        Place(kind: 10, cell_x: 6, cell_y: 1),       // 1: HTTP HANDLER, 3x3
        Place(kind: 7, cell_x: 10, cell_y: 5),       // 2: SINK, Debug by default
        DrawBelt(cells: [(7, 4), (7, 5), (8, 5), (9, 5)]),                // 3
        Dock(belt: 3, endpoint: Tail, node: 1, port: 2),
        Dock(belt: 3, endpoint: Head, node: 2, port: 0),
        Configure(node: 0, config: Endpoint(path: "/hello")),
        Configure(node: 1, config: Factory(source: r#"// greet the name in the body
export default function (input, ctx) {
  const { name } =
    JSON.parse(input.body);
  ctx.command({
    status: name ? 200 : 400,
    headers: {},
    body: name ? "hello " + name
               : "send a name",
  }, 0);
}"#)),
        DrawWire(from_node: 0, from_port: 1, to_node: 1, to_port: 0),
    ],
    script: [
        At(tick: 40, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/hello", body: r#"{"name":"Ada"}"#)),
        At(tick: 120, input: Request(route: 0, method: "POST", path: "/endpoint/hello", body: r#"{}"#)),
    ],
    captions: [
        // Measured: the Handler runs on 42 and 122, and each reply is back at the Route a tick later.
        Caption(tick: 42, highlight: 1, text: "This request's body has the name Ada, so the Handler replies with status 200 and the body hello Ada."),
        Caption(tick: 122, highlight: 1, text: "This request has no name, so the Handler replies with status 400 and the body send a name."),
    ],
    executor: Executor(default: Reply(after_ticks: 1), rules: []),
    view: View(fit: Board),
    end_tick: 200,
)
